# .trivyignore — exclude HIGH-severity CVEs in upstream-bundled components
# we don't control. molecule-ci#38 follow-up (Trivy gate too strict for
# templates carrying upstream binary distributions).
#
# Scope:
#   - 100 linux-libc-dev kernel-header CVEs from python:3.11-slim
#     (Debian-side; kernel headers don't ship binary code, kernel CVEs
#     don't apply to this artifact in a container — the host kernel
#     determines exposure)
#   - 1 picomatch CVE from hermes-agent's bundled Node 22 install
#     (NousResearch upstream rebuild required)
#   - 9 golang stdlib CVEs from a vendored Go binary in the hermes
#     install bundle (cloudflared/gosu — upstream rebuild required)
#
# Re-audit 2026-08-01 — by then Debian should have shipped a
# python:3.11-slim rebuild with newer linux-libc-dev, AND NousResearch
# may have shipped a hermes-agent installer with refreshed bundles.
# Walk this list, drop any CVE that's no longer in the latest scan.
#
# Long-term fix in molecule-ci: add per-template skip-dirs/skip-files
# for /usr/include/linux + /home/agent/.hermes (vendored upstream),
# tracked separately.

